In article <7616@batcomputer.tn.cornell.edu> mll@honesty.tn.cornell.edu (Mighty Atom) writes:

   Here are a couple of suggestions for 3.0:

   When you have a polymorph control ring and are asked what to turn into
   you should only be able to turn into something that you have already
   encountered.

I like the idea, and would go even further. The player should only be
be able to polymorph into a monster, which he has already killed. This
should include random polymorph. If he want to be a Dragon, he should
prove himself worth it first.

It should be easy to implement, insert something like this somewhere
in polyself():

{
	int count = 100;

	do {
		mntmp = rn2(CMNUM);
		count--;
	} while(count > 0 && u.nr_killed[mntmp] == 0);

	if(count < 1) mntmp = ACID_BLOB; /* Or whatever... */
}

Maybe it should be easier to polymorph into a monster you have killed
several times many times. 

   Another more tentative suggestion is changing the dungeon floorplan
   size to fit the window.

No. It would either make the game more difficult or easier, and the
game should not depend on the size of your screen.

The right way to do it, is to make the screen be a window to a
possibly larger game level, like in moria. But this would require a
major rewrite.

